3a. Describe the problem(s) that you are attempting to solve.
The invention holistically solves a set of four profound and interdependent challenges that define the limits of current and planned telecommunications networks:



Escalating 6G Complexity: Future 6G networks, with projected connection densities of 10 million devices/km² and terabit-per-second data rates, will be of unprecedented complexity. Traditional management systems, even those with conventional AI, are insufficient to manage this scale in real-time.



The Imminent Quantum Threat: The rapid advancement of quantum computing poses a catastrophic threat to current public-key cryptography (e.g., RSA, ECC). This creates an urgent need for a new security paradigm to protect long-term data from "harvest now, decrypt later" attacks.



The "Achilles' Heel" of QKD: While Quantum Key Distribution (QKD) offers provable security, its practical deployment is critically hampered by its reliance on "trusted relays" for range extension. The compromise of a single one of these nodes can invalidate the security of the entire network, making it a brittle and vulnerable architecture.



Limitations of Conventional AI: The AI/ML systems used in 5G are based on power-hungry, high-latency von Neumann architectures (e.g., GPUs). They are too slow, energy-intensive, and reactive to control a 6G system at the required microsecond timescales or secure a quantum network in real-time.



4. Describe your solution and how it is an improvement over previous approaches to solve the problem(s).
The solution is a holistic, tri-layered network architecture that natively integrates an ultra-fast 6G Transport Layer, an ultra-secure Quantum Security Layer (QSL), and an ultra-intelligent Neuromorphic Cognitive Orchestration Layer (NCOL). This architecture is a fundamental improvement over prior art because its layers are designed to solve the identified problems synergistically.


Solving 6G Complexity & AI Inefficiency: The NCOL, built on a distributed fabric of brain-inspired neuromorphic processors running Spiking Neural Networks (SNNs), replaces conventional AI. Its event-driven, low-power, and microsecond-latency processing provides the real-time cognitive control necessary to manage the 6G layer and enables new paradigms like 

Emergent Intent-Based Networking and Predictive Self-Healing.




Solving the Quantum Threat & QKD Vulnerability: The QSL uses a hybrid of Post-Quantum Cryptography (PQC) for baseline security and QKD for high-value data. Crucially, the invention introduces a 

Neuromorphic-Managed Trusted Relay System. The NCOL assigns a dynamic "Trust Score" to each QKD relay in real-time by detecting subtle operational anomalies. It then intelligently routes quantum keys along the demonstrably most secure path, transforming QKD's critical vulnerability into a resilient, self-healing security fabric.




5. Describe the technical and commercial benefits of your invention (over prior approaches to solve the problem), including any disadvantages that may be derived by not pursuing the invention for AT&T.

Technical Benefits:


Microsecond Decision Latency: The NCOL enables control loops that are orders of magnitude faster than conventional AI (microseconds vs. milliseconds/seconds), which is essential for 6G URLLC services.


Ultra-Low Power Consumption: Neuromorphic processors are orders of magnitude more energy-efficient than GPUs for real-time monitoring tasks, leading to greener and more sustainable network operations.



Real-Time Adaptability: The SNNs' ability to learn continuously via synaptic plasticity allows the network to adapt to novel conditions without needing to be reprogrammed or retrained offline.


Proactive, Real-Time Security: The invention solves the QKD trusted relay vulnerability by transforming trust from a static assumption into a dynamic, continuously verified metric. It can proactively isolate threats before a compromise occurs.




True Self-Evolution: The Quantum-State-Aware Digital Twin allows the system to safely simulate and pre-validate complex network changes, enabling a continuous cycle of autonomous improvement.


Commercial Benefits:


New High-Margin Revenue Streams: Creates entirely new service categories (QSaaS, NOaaS) that command premium pricing and address urgent market needs in security and automation.




Significant OPEX Reduction: The NCOL's autonomous management and predictive self-healing capabilities will dramatically reduce operational costs associated with network monitoring, maintenance, and manual configuration.


Durable Competitive Advantage: Provides a 5-10 year strategic advantage by establishing leadership in the 6G and quantum networking eras. Failure to pursue this would risk ceding the future of secure, intelligent networking to competitors and becoming a provider of "dumb pipe" connectivity.


Unlocking New Industries: Enables mission-critical applications in telesurgery, autonomous transportation, and city-scale digital twins that are not feasible with current technology, opening up entirely new markets.

